    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Description\n\nAs I understand, currently it is possible with predicate function:\n```lua\npredicate = function()\n    if vim.o.buftype ~= \"\" then return false end\n    return not scope.body.is_incomplete\nend,\n```\n\nBut isn't autocommand still be there for that filetypes/buftypes? If it is possible currently, maybe add this to the docs?",
